THE LID PACK'S BQ4050 WORDS UNDER A CURRENT-SCALE CALIBRATION OF k = 2 (gauge_scale.py, stream a1elec, MESHSAT-1357)
PROTOTYPE DESIGN; AI arithmetic; every true value a design requirement, NOT_YET_TESTED. Source: TI SLUUAQ3A (sha256 525d16b2bdee44e5...),
Table 14-1 as its text layer prints it; the page is the PDF page, which is the manual's printed page number.

1. WHY k: the two design-capacity rows and the pack
   0x444d Design Capacity mAh      max  32767 mAh : the pack's  40200 mAh is ABOVE its maximum; at k = 2 it is written  20100 (61.3 percent of the maximum)
   0x444f Design Capacity cWh      max  32767 cWh : the pack's  57888 cWh is ABOVE its maximum; at k = 2 it is written  28944 (88.3 percent of the maximum)
   With the specification's typical 3.45 Ah a cell the pack is 41,400 mAh and 59,616 cWh: written 20,700 and 29,808 at k = 2.
   k = 2 is the smallest integer that fits both; the internal current range of an I2 word (-32,768 to 32,767) then spans
   -65.5 to +65.5 A true, above the pack path's 25 A blade, so no current the path can carry is clipped.

2. THE CALIBRATION WORDS (written by the gauge's own current calibration, not by hand)
   0x4006 CC Gain          type F4, range 0.1 to 4.0, TI default 3.58422 (page 185)
   0x400a Capacity Gain    type F4, range 29800.0 to 1190000.0, TI default 1069035.256 (page 185)
   Procedure (SLUUBF9 3.3.3, TI's EVM guide; SLUA760 2.3 for the scaled case): apply a known current, enter its value
   in Applied Current. For k = 2 the value entered is half the applied true current (apply -4000 mA through the pack
   path, enter -2000; SLUA760's own example). The firmware
   then computes both gains so that its unit is 2 mA; their ratio stays TI's (1069035.256 / 3.58422 = 298261.6).
   The manual does not state how CC Gain relates to the sense resistance, so its value after calibration is READ BACK
   at commissioning and must lie inside the row's range; that read-back is a bench item, not shown here.

