   every scaled word has a stated true value and its written value lies inside its row's range; addresses in the
   true-value table that Table 14-1 does not list with a scaled unit: none

4. NOT SCALED (the other 322 rows by unit): % 27, 0.01% 1, 0.10% 1, 0.1°C 20, 0.1°K 7, 116 nV 1, 2h 12, cycles 13, date 1, events 14, mV 77, min 3, s 71, steps 2, °C 13, µs 3, (no unit) 56
   Voltages (COV, CUV, the charge voltages, Design Voltage 14400 mV), temperatures, times and bit fields are written as
   the base's image writes them. The AFE words (AOLD, ASCC, ASCD thresholds in AFE Protection Control and their codes)
   are voltages across the real shunt: set on R10's true 2 mOhm, as board P's, because board PL's path limits are board P's.

5. WHAT THE HOST MUST SCALE (k = 2): every SBS or MAC value in mA, mAh, 10 mWh or cW: Current(), AverageCurrent(),
   RemainingCapacity(), FullChargeCapacity(), DesignCapacity(), ChargingCurrent(), MaxError is a percent (not scaled),
   RunTimeToEmpty and the other times are computed by the gauge from its own consistent units (not scaled), the
   Lifetimes and PF Status current records, and any value it writes (none in the kit's contract). ChargingCurrent()
   is multiplied by k BEFORE the host writes U3B's ChargeCurrent (FW-A02's lid row, CHARGER.md). Voltages, cell voltages,
   temperatures, RSOC and flags are not scaled. The marker: Manufacturer Info Block A (0x4041 onward, page 194) carries
   the ASCII text 'IPSCALE2' and the host refuses the lid gauge's currents and capacities until it has read it.

END.
